-- title:
--   Unit principle on the node annulus of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that is trivial modulo $M/p$, and the hypothesis `hj` that `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion function field of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP` package for these data. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a map $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, together with compatible maps $t_\kappa : O \to \kappa(A)$, $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\iota_A : O \to A$ (the coherence conditions are those displayed). Let $n$ be a point of the pullback of the two branch maps $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$, write $x_n$ for its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by the branch $0$ map and `bcMap`, let $e \ge 1$, and let $U$ be an open of $X_O =$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` containing $x_n$, equipped with a morphism $f$ from $U$ to $\operatorname{Spec} O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)$ over $O$ such that: both coordinates vanish at $y \in U$ exactly when $y$ maps to $x_n$; over $x_n$ the stalk maps of $f$ are flat, carry the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induce isomorphisms of residue fields; $f$ is étale on a neighbourhood of each point over $x_n$; and the vanishing loci of $X_1$, resp. $X_0$, are exactly the images of the branch $0$, resp. branch $1$, maps. Let $\mathrm{pr}_J$ be the base change of $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ to $X_O$ along $j_O$, let $g_v, g_u \in \Gamma(X_O, \iota(\top))$ be the pullbacks along $f$ of the classes of $X_1$ and $X_0$, assume the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ lies in the preimage of $\iota(\top)$, let $\mathrm{read}$ be the resulting ring homomorphism from $\Gamma(X_O, \iota(\top))$ to $\overline{X_H}$'s function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` (apply $\mathrm{pr}_J^\sharp$, then $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}^\sharp$, then the germ at the generic point, then $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$), and set $\mathrm{param} = \mathrm{read}(g_v)$. Say that a place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with surjective map to its residue field lies in the tube if there is a section $s : \operatorname{Spec} A \to U$ over $\iota_A$ whose generic point is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point attached to $W$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ and whose closed point maps to $x_n$. The assertion: for every nonzero $g$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` such that $\operatorname{ord}_W g = 0$ for all such $W$ and $s$, there are $m \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $c \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}^\times$ with $W.\mathrm{evalAt}(g)\, c^{-1} (W.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{param}))^{-m}$ lying in $A$ and a unit there, for every such $W$ and $s$.
--
--   This is the substantive clause of the unit principle for the node annulus of $X_H(M)$ at $p$: a function with neither zero nor pole on the tube of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points reducing to the node has, up to a constant, a single slope in the annulus parameter read off from the étale crossing chart. It feeds the construction of the annulus attached to the node, where the modulus is identified with $p^e$ and the parameter with $\mathrm{read}(g_v)$, within the semistable-reduction analysis of $X_H(M)$ at $p$.
